<section>
  <h1>How to Use HEIC Converter Pro</h1>

  <ol>
    <li>Open <strong>HEIC Converter Pro</strong>.</li>

    <li>Tap <strong>Select HEIC/HEIF Photos</strong>.</li>

    <li>
      Choose one or more HEIC or HEIF photos from your photo library, then tap
      <strong>Done</strong>.
    </li>

    <li>
      Your selected HEIC/HEIF photos will appear in the <strong>Photos</strong> section.
    </li>

    <li>
      Choose your output format:
      <ul>
        <li><strong>JPG</strong> for smaller, widely compatible photos.</li>
        <li><strong>PNG</strong> for lossless image output.</li>
      </ul>
    </li>

    <li>
      If JPG is selected, adjust the <strong>JPG Quality</strong> slider if desired.
      Lower quality usually creates smaller files. Higher quality keeps more detail
      but may create larger files.
    </li>

    <li>Tap <strong>Convert Selected Photos</strong>.</li>

    <li>
      After conversion, the Results screen will show:
      <ul>
        <li>How many photos were converted</li>
        <li>How many non-HEIC/HEIF photos were skipped</li>
        <li>Thumbnails of converted photos</li>
        <li>Original and converted file sizes</li>
      </ul>
    </li>

    <li>Tap <strong>OK</strong> to return to the main screen.</li>

    <li>
      Converted photos are saved to your Photos app in an album named
      <strong>HEIC Converted</strong>.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Notes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The app only converts HEIC and HEIF images.</li>
    <li>JPG, PNG, screenshots, and other image types are skipped.</li>
    <li>All conversion happens on your device.</li>
    <li>Your photos are never uploaded or sent anywhere.</li>
  </ul>
</section>
